  "classdef": {
    "_comment": "Node-category classDef roles for generators that emit their own 'classDef name fill:...,stroke:...' lines inside a <pre class=\"mermaid\"> block. Not used by mermaid.js itself. Every fill draws from the --data-1..4 ramp, never from the prose accents (--pink, --green, --orange): those already carry a meaning in body copy (h1, inline code, aside bar), and the data ramp exists precisely so a diagram category cannot borrow it. stroke is --purple for every role, and color is the text that lands on the fill: --surface here, because the dark ramp is pale. THIS SET IS DARK ONLY. A page that follows the reader's appearance must not emit classDef hex at all, because a fence has no CSS to read and one hex cannot serve both palettes; emit classdefLight only on a page locked to light.",
    "repo":  { "fill": "#ec80cb", "stroke": "#aa8cdb", "color": "#282a36", "from": "--data-2" },
    "ext":   { "fill": "#96bef0", "stroke": "#aa8cdb", "color": "#282a36", "from": "--data-1" },
    "store": { "fill": "#4bd1a0", "stroke": "#aa8cdb", "color": "#282a36", "from": "--data-3" },
    "queue": { "fill": "#bcc267", "stroke": "#aa8cdb", "color": "#282a36", "from": "--data-4" }
  },
  "classdefLight": {
    "_comment": "The same four roles projected through the @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) palette, for a page locked to light the way samples/light.html is. The light ramp is mid-tone rather than pale, so the text on the fill inverts: color is --on-surface, which measures 4.98 to 5.10:1 against the four fills where --surface measures 3.45 to 3.53:1. Same role names and same 'from' tokens as classdef, resolved through the light block; palette-check.py check 2 gates both sets and fails if the role sets diverge.",
    "repo":  { "fill": "#cf5cae", "stroke": "#804cc2", "color": "#161616", "from": "--data-2" },
    "ext":   { "fill": "#3c88e4", "stroke": "#804cc2", "color": "#161616", "from": "--data-1" },
    "store": { "fill": "#349874", "stroke": "#804cc2", "color": "#161616", "from": "--data-3" },
    "queue": { "fill": "#878c48", "stroke": "#804cc2", "color": "#161616", "from": "--data-4" }
